<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech ZB Podil sees higher 1996 result.</title>
<headline>Czech ZB Podil sees higher 1996 result.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results showed Czech unit trust Zivnobanka Podilovy Fond 1996 calendar year net profit rose to 33.786 million crowns from 20.391 million, the fund's manager ZB Trust said on Thursday.</p>
<p>(In millions of crowns)</p>
<p> net result		33.786 profit vs   20.391 profit</p>
<p> operating result	25.104 loss   vs   15.956 loss</p>
<p> financial yield    1,151.181	  vs   620.826</p>
<p> financial costs    1,092.291	  vs   578.176</p>
<p> total assets	 1,158.590	  vs   936.199</p>
<p>Note. The fund has not yet disclosed dividend plans on 1996 profit. It paid an 11.40 crown per share gross dividend on 1995 profit.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
